  "selectedConclusions": [
    "9:9 is declared argc6. Native adapter reads extra low DWORD scratch slots through15, but the immediate leaf reads only local element0 corresponding to operand5; argc16 is not justified.",
    "9:25 positive operand2 is a signed loop batch count before cooperative yield, default10. Source-pointer equality bypasses rebuild and rotation/count changes. Other phase yields remain; this is not a time duration or a scheduler safety proof.",
    "9:22/23 write camera eye/target inputs. 9:24 invokes the captured matrix rebuild; 9:32 mode0 chooses horizontal FOV, other values vertical, using radians with tanf/atanf and original512/416 constants.",
    "9:18 queues child retirement and clears binding fields. Native VM_THREAD destruction queues its base VM; task cleanup frees the thread separately. The retirement drain can call VM destruction and its exit code before allocator release.",
    "9:27 NULL target skips per-object attachment stores, and a NULL effective camera skips its per-object store. Clearing existing attachment is not implied by supplying NULL here.",
    "The remaining annotations keep native type/field/slot descriptions where gameplay meanings, model backends, resources or lifetimes are not established."
